\f1 Description of the show -One stage only, Elvises on stage playing all the instruments, strobe lighting, glittering backdrop, and karate dance moves etc but there is a line of Elvises waiting their turn to sing.The crowd is a mixure of a few Cloudborne and the rest are Elvi. All very festive and friendly.The Elvises living in the apartments dance and sing along and are a part of the whole show, no matter where you look, there\'92s an Elvis doing something outrageous\'85.)\
\pard\pardeftab720\sl360\slmult1\sa160\partightenfactor0
\cf3 \
\'91Are they..\'92Sarah tried to speak but was cut off.\
\'91Yes, they are all Elvises, even the females\'92 Cracker smiled broadly. \'91This is the real thing.\'92\
\'91I have never heard any of these songs before.\'92 Sarah craned her head back and forth, listening intently. \'91Just fantastic, phenomenal, extraordinary..\'92\
\'91They make the songs up as they go, too.\'92Cracker said.\'91They are musical geniuses. Every one of them.\'92\
\'91Why haven\'92t I heard this music before?\'92\
\'91\'92When they first introduced, I think the idea was anyone could have their own domestic Elvis.Like a servant come entertainer.\'92\
\'91That sounds pretty handy, but it doesn\'92t explain why music this sublime hasn\'92t permeated throughout the PTD.\'92 Sarah replied.\
\'91What do you think happens when you drop a talented, charismatic, handsome and virile young Elvis into a domestic setting?\'92 Cracker didn\'92t wait for a response. \'91You get Elvises seducing every female in the house and Elvines seducing every male in the house. Not a recipe for domestic bliss.\'92 \cf2 (I thought here to say the Elvines were used as sex toys or rented out, but that took me off course. I mention Elvis/Elvine brothels later.)\cf3 \
\'91So they all ended up here?\'92 Sarah said. \
\'91To work in hospitality and sing in crappy bars for tips.\'92 Cracker lamented. \'91They find it deeply offensive to their true nature.\'92\
 \'91I\'92ve only seen them singing covers in clubs and karaoke bars.\'92\
\'91This is where the Elvi run free and their true nature revealed.\'92 Cracker said. \
\'91
\f2\i Where I\'92ll be free to have and honest heart
\f1\i0 .\'92 Sarah quoted under her breath. \'91It seems to make them very happy.\'92 \
\'91They do this every Sunday, religiously.\'92 Cracker said. \
\'91You would never see such a display of joy above the layer, that\'92s for sure.\'92 Sarah replied.\'91The Airborne, what a miserable bunch.\'92\
\'91You don\'92t say.\'92 Cracker scanned the crowd. \'91Judging by how drunk these punters are, we\'92ve got a bit of catching up to do. What\'92s your poison? If you ask politely you can get almost anything from an Elvis.\'92 \
\'91I\'92ll go with a beer.\'92 Sarah looked about. \'91Where do we go?\'92\
\'91Grab a waiter.\'92 Cracker smirked. \'91They\'92re easy to spot. They look like Elvis.\'92\
\
\cf2 (To tie in your idea of the Elvi \'91hearing\'92 songs from other universes, there is a collective-unconsciousness that cause all the Elvi to hear \'91archetypical tunes\'92.In a competitive battle, they play the songs and each has a turn with their own lyrics (sometimes made up as they go).When they get drunk enough they argue over lyrics and it can violent.The lyrics are all great and the songs sound good, but they all have an uneasy feeling something, generally, is not quite right. I will try to get some lyrics going, at least the names of a few songs.)\cf3 \
\
Sarah chanced eye contact with an Elvine who nodded and casually strolled over. \
\
\'91Hello, Elvine.I\'92m Sarah and this is\'85\
\'91Cracker!\'92Elvine took two paces jumped high, hugging him tightly with both arms and legs. \'91Didn\'92t you see me over there?\'92\
\'91I thought that was you,\'92 Cracker lied, \'91but it\'92s was hard to tell in this light.\'92 \
Elvine laughed and craned her head around and looked at a bemused Sarah.She climbed down from Cracker and straightened her tassels.\'91My sincerest apologies, Sarah.\'92\
\'91That is very thoughtful of you, Elvine, but there is no need for any apology.\'92 Sarah smiled graciously. \
\'91Who\'92s up for a drink?\'92 Elvine clapped her hands together. \'91The first round is on me, I want to see the legend in action.\'92\
\'91No, I\'92m not out for a big-one tonight.\'92 Cracker pleaded. From past experience he knew he would get more free beers if he pretended he didn\'92t want them.\
\'91Two beers each for starters?\'92 Elvine inquired.\'91You know, Sarah. He can drink any Elvi under the table.\'92Elvine turned, took three steps and vanished into the writhing mass of Elvi.\
